quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  7,1,"Alif, Lam, Mim, Sad."
  7,2,"(This is) a Book revealed to you. So, let there be no constriction in your breast on its account (because of the unpleasant response of the disbelievers)—so you may warn (them) with it. And (it is) a Reminder for the believers."
  7,3,"(Believers!) Follow what has been sent down to you from your Lord, and do not follow (the self-proclaimed) guardians besides Him. How seldom do you accept advice?"
  7,4,How many towns have We destroyed? Our punishment came upon them at night or while they were taking a midday nap.
  7,5,"When Our punishment overtook them, they could say nothing but cry: ‘Indeed we were wrongdoers.’"
  7,6,"We shall certainly question those to whom the messengers were sent, and We shall surely ask the messengers (too)."
  7,7,"Then We shall surely relate to them (all their affairs) from (Our) knowledge, for We had never been absent."
  7,8,"And the weighing (of deeds) on that Day is true. As for those whose scales (of good deeds) are heavy, they are the ones who shall be prosperous."
  7,9,"As for those whose scales (of good deeds) are light, they are the ones who have ruined their souls, for they used to treat Our revelations wrongfully."
  7,10,And We have surely established you on the earth and provided in it (different) means of livelihood for you. How seldom do you give thanks?
  7,11,"Indeed, We created you, then We shaped you. Then We said to the angels: ‘Prostrate yourselves before Adam.’ So they (all) prostrated except Iblis. He was not among those who prostrated."
